# `yo fix <path> --migrate explicit-copy` lists, and never rewrites, a copy
# inside the member of a `Clone` impl
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-22-explicit-copy-migration-deepens-a-sharing-clone-impl.md).
# `Tree.clone` shares its `kids` handle on purpose, as `AstExpr`'s does in
# src/expr.yo; the migration used to rewrite it to `kids.clone()`, which made
# every clone deep and the run print `0`. `Bag(T)`'s generic impl (evaluated
# through `_c2_eval_inner_field`) shares `items` the same way. Each impl is
# recognized as the prelude's `Clone` by identity, not by the member's name.
# `tags.push(label)` outside the impls is still cloned. The trailing `build run` runs the
# migrated program: its `1 n 1 1` line is the behavior the rewrite must keep.
# stdout_keep drops the build chatter.
stdout_keep=^(fix:|[0-9]+ n [0-9]+ [0-9]+$)
timeout=600
